title: 'Mod playbooks, checkpoint 10: founder approves the naming convention, mod-authoring skills and versioning; Arky designing for S0'
summary: |-
  The founder approved three things:
  (1) The standardized mod naming. Mod id = publisher.name; first-party publisher = gnomon; git owner = publisher; folders = local; MCP server gm-<publisher>-<name>; env PUBLISHER_NAME_*; events mod.<publisher>.<name>.*. neurons-brain becomes gnomon.neurons.
  (2) Mod-authoring skills (from-folder, from-api, offers, check), as T-2026-10-20-012, sequenced after the O1 dogfood.
  (3) Versioning, so mods survive large changes and new formats as Gnomon evolves:
  - mod semver
  - git installs pinned to url#commit
  - the kernel accepts the current and previous major manifest/offer-spec formats via pure load-time upgraders (never rewriting on disk) and refuses future majors with "needs Gnomon ≥ X"
  - an engines compatibility declaration checked at install and at load
  - a format upgrade is not a widening unless the effective grants grow
  Plan: Arky designs naming and versioning against the code. Aegis reviews (publisher spoofing, homoglyphs, case, alias abuse). Fold it into S0 before merge, then rebase S1/S2/S3 at integration. Founder: "continue down this road".
